Corrected message:

Accept site URLs with or without a trailing slash

With trailingSlash 'never', the English home link ('/') still had a
slash, so switching back to English raised the same "did you mean"
dev-server warning the other locales had. GitHub Pages serves both
forms, so use 'ignore' and make every locale link directory-style
('/', '/es/', ...).

Also make the site deploy workflow run on pushes to the 'website'
branch instead of 'main'.
